# Codex Scope Guide

This file is scoped to this directory. Source of truth: CLAUDE.md in the same folder.

# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## App: `apps/web`

Next.js 14 App Router frontend for TopShelf Teaching. Talks to `@topshelf/api-server` via REST. Uses Zustand for auth and challenge state.

```bash
pnpm dev        # Next.js dev server
pnpm build      # production build
pnpm test       # Vitest (unit/hook tests)
pnpm typecheck
```

## Routing

```
src/app/
  (app)/            # protected route group — dashboard, content, learn, settings, profile
  (legal)/          # public — privacy, terms, contact, support
  auth/             # public — login, signup, verify-email, forgot-password, reset-password, oauth-complete
  kitchen/          # kitchen simulation domain
```

Route protection is enforced via middleware or layout-level auth checks using `useAuthStore`. The `(app)` group redirects unauthenticated users to `/auth/login`.

## Auth Pattern

`useAuthStore` (Zustand + `localStorage` persistence) is the client-side auth source of truth:

```ts
import { useAuthStore } from '@/stores/auth-store';
const { user, accessToken, isAuthenticated, setAuthFromResponse, logout } = useAuthStore();
```

`setAuthFromResponse(response)` hydrates user + tokens from login/refresh API responses. `isAuthenticated()` returns false if either token or user is missing — check this before protected API calls.

Tokens are injected into every `api.*` call automatically by `src/lib/api/client.ts` (reads `accessToken` from the store). Do not manually add `Authorization` headers in route components.

## API Layer

```ts
import { learnerApi } from '@/lib/api/learner';
import { contentApi } from '@/lib/api/content';
import { badgeApi } from '@/lib/api/badge';
// etc.
```

Each module wraps `api.get/post/put/patch/delete` from `src/lib/api/client.ts`. Return type is always `Promise<T>` where `T` is the typed response shape. All route → backend contracts are documented in comments at the top of each `src/lib/api/*.ts` file.

**`learnerApi` endpoints:**

| Method                                  | Description                                             |
| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `getStats()`                            | Aggregate stats: time, blocks, mastery, packs, sessions |
| `getStates()`                           | All per-pack learner states                             |
| `getState(packId)`                      | Single learner state detail                             |
| `getProgress(packId)`                   | State + last 50 events                                  |
| `getWeeklyGoal()`                       | Weekly time target + completion                         |
| `updateWeeklyGoal(minutes)`             | Update weekly target                                    |
| `startSession(packId, deviceInfo?)`     | Start session, returns sessionId                        |
| `recordEvent(sessionId, event)`         | Record progress event                                   |
| `endSession(sessionId)`                 | End session                                             |
| `getTeachingGuidance(sessionId, opts?)` | Engine-backed teaching response                         |
| `getRecentSessions(limit?)`             | Session list                                            |

## Stores

```
src/stores/
  auth-store.ts       # user, accessToken, refreshToken, hydration, logout
  challenge-store.ts  # kitchen challenge state (active challenge, phase, score)
```

Do not store server-fetched data in Zustand — use `useState`/`useEffect` or a data-fetching hook. Stores are for session-level client state only.

## Kitchen UI Components

```
src/components/kitchen/
  DirtyHandTimer     # compliance countdown
  MasteryRing        # circular mastery progress indicator
  RecipeCard         # step-by-step recipe display
  TicketQueue        # order ticket management
  TempGauge          # temperature compliance indicator
  SafetyAlert        # food safety trigger display
  GradeBadge         # session grade badge
```

These components receive data from `challenge-store` and render kitchen domain state. They do not call the API directly — the kitchen route pages orchestrate data flow.

## Environment Variables

`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` — API base URL injected into `src/lib/api/client.ts`. Must be set in `.env.local` for local development. Production value set via deployment config.
